{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And his anger burned, etc.</b> The reason is that she let slip from her mouth a word of curse when she said ״I am dead,״ and the words of the righteous make an impact even when spoken in such a manner. Go out and learn (Genesis Rabbah 74:9) from the fact that he himself cursed on a condition, etc.; therefore his anger burned. And for this reason the verse is precise in saying <b>with Rachel</b> — meaning, on her account; also because she said ״Give me,״ etc., and did not say: pray for me."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:44:59.959850621Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}